<title>POLAND: POLISH BROAD MONEY FALLS 0.4 PCT IN JAN 1-20 - NBP.</title>
<headline>POLISH BROAD MONEY FALLS 0.4 PCT IN JAN 1-20 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money fell by 581.5</p>
<p>million zlotys, or 0.4 percent, in January 1-20 period to 134.9</p>
<p>billion after a 5.1 percent rise in December, preliminary</p>
<p>central bank figures showed.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		    Jan 1-20   December 1996    </p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)	     -0.4	  5.1	</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   134.91     135.49	   </p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	23.76	23.36	   </p>
<p>  National currency		     111.15     112.12	   </p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    22.71	23.56	   </p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    82.48	81.09</p>
<p>NOTE: Starting from January, 1 1997 the NBP changed the</p>
<p>methodology of calculating monetary aggregates. Data for end of</p>
<p>December 1996 are estimations presented in the new comparable</p>
<p>format. -- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
